---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Copy objects on their board, or with --into onto another board; the copies get new ids and keep their content.
They go to a free corner unless --at gives the corner of the copied group. Images and files are uploaded again for another board. It prints one line per copy with @N and its link.

USAGE
  holst object cp <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name

FLAGS
      --object object   An object, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
      --into board      Copy onto this board: id, link or part of its name; the same board by default
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --at x,y          The top-left corner of the copied group in board units; a free corner by default
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o cp "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --object e5f6a7b8
  $ holst o cp "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --at 800,0
  $ holst o cp "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --into "Retro"

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
